WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:02.635 align:start size:88% position:13%
- And I started the race
to run for Congress.

00:00:02.635 --> 00:00:04.404
And part of that reason was
because of Maxine Waters,

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:07.007
trying to get help
with my VA benefits.

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was sleeping
outside the lighthouse

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:09.943
at Ranchos Palos Verdes

00:00:09.943 --> 00:00:11.578
and I was going to her
office every other day

00:00:11.578 --> 00:00:12.946
trying to get help.

00:00:12.946 --> 00:00:14.481 align:start size:94% position:6%
I filled out job
applications, internships,

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.515
I even brought her flowers,

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:17.350
and I was met with silence.

00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:19.119
And that really made me upset

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.254 align:start size:97% position:3%
because a majority of the
people who live on the streets

00:00:21.254 --> 00:00:24.591
are homeless veterans and
60% of them are Black.

00:00:24.591 --> 00:00:25.992 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so you have
this lady who says,

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.861
"Well, I'm pro Black
this, pro Black that,

00:00:27.861 --> 00:00:29.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
I fight for Black people,
all of this stuff."

00:00:29.496 --> 00:00:31.031
And here I am, a young Black man

00:00:31.031 --> 00:00:32.265
and you're not fighting for me.

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:35.168
We have 44,000 homeless
people in the streets.

00:00:35.168 --> 00:00:37.203
60% of 'em are Black veterans.

00:00:37.203 --> 00:00:38.738
You're not fighting
for those people.

00:00:38.738 --> 00:00:41.074
So which Black people
are you fighting for?

00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:43.943
(purposeful music)

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.417 line:0%
- I'm Dave Rubin and this
is "The Rubin Report."

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:54.154 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
We're doing a mini interview
today with Joe Collins.

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:56.022 align:start size:88% position:13%
Joe is a U.S. Navy
veteran and a Republican

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:59.793 align:start size:97% position:3%
running for Congress in
Los Angeles' 43rd district.

00:00:59.793 --> 00:01:01.661
Looking to unseat Maxine Waters,

00:01:01.661 --> 00:01:05.098
who's been in Congress
for a cool 44 years.

00:01:05.098 --> 00:01:08.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
I caught wind of Joe after
his viral campaign ad

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.869
that I'm sure many
of you have seen.

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.738 align:start size:88% position:13%
So we're gonna show
you just a bite of that

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:14.107
and then get right to
the interview with Joe.

00:01:14.107 --> 00:01:15.275
Here we go.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:88% position:13%
(intense hip hop)
(cash register ringing)

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:19.646 line:0%
- I'm Joe Collins.

00:01:19.646 --> 00:01:21.915 line:0%
I'm running for Congress
against Maxine Waters.

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.716 line:0%
Do you know where
I am right now?

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:27.187 line:0%
Maxine Waters's $6
million mansion.

00:01:27.187 --> 00:01:29.489 line:0%
(cash register ringing) Do you
know where I'm not right now?

00:01:29.489 --> 00:01:30.924 line:0%
Maxine Waters' district.

00:01:30.924 --> 00:01:32.392 line:0%
Yup, that's right.

00:01:32.392 --> 00:01:35.495 line:0%
Maxine does not live in
her district, but I do.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:37.530 line:0%
I was born right
here in South LA,

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.933 line:0%
in the place Maxine
refuses to live.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:42.302 line:0%
Maxine Waters does
not drink our water.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:43.970 line:0%
She does not breathe our air.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.339 line:0%
And while she sits
here in her mansion,

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.874 line:0%
our district is in ruins.

00:01:47.874 --> 00:01:48.975 line:0%
Let me show you.

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.778 line:0%
(intense hip hop)

00:01:54.781 --> 00:01:56.182 line:0%
This is South LA.

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:57.750 line:0%
I was born here.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.919 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
I grew up on 104th
and Normandie.

00:01:59.919 --> 00:02:03.223 line:0%
Maxine Waters has been
in office for 44 years.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:05.525 line:0%
Has anything got
better around here?

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.994 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
I can tell you firsthand
that it hasn't.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:10.797 line:0%
I survived a drive-by
shooting in this house

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:12.065 line:0%
when I was a child.

00:02:12.065 --> 00:02:15.602 line:0%
Gangs, drugs, violence,
that was my upbringing.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:17.137 line:0%
And where was Maxine Waters?

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:19.038 line:0%
Nowhere to be found.

00:02:19.038 --> 00:02:20.773
- Joe, how's it going today?

00:02:21.641 --> 00:02:22.876
- Good, how are you?

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:24.444
- I'm doin' well,
I'm doin' well.

00:02:24.444 --> 00:02:26.913
So look, you put that ad up

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:31.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
and much like the Kim
Klacik ad, it caught fire.

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:32.952
Are new people heading your way?

00:02:32.952 --> 00:02:36.189
Do you feel like you have
some momentum right now?

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:37.290 line:0%
- Oh yeah.

00:02:37.290 --> 00:02:39.726 line:0%
You know, success leaves clues

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:41.227
and we saw what Kim did

00:02:41.227 --> 00:02:44.631
and we absolutely, you
know, did one of our own

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.634
and people have been coming
our way for a very long time.

00:02:47.634 --> 00:02:49.269
We've been getting
a lot of support.

00:02:49.269 --> 00:02:50.870 align:start size:84% position:16%
But I think one of
the biggest things was

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.439
we had to actually shine a
light on how Maxine lives

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.308
compared to how we
live in the district.

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.911 align:start size:84% position:16%
And we absolutely
nailed it with that.

00:02:57.911 --> 00:02:59.112
- Yeah, all right,

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:00.914 align:start size:88% position:13%
so before get to a
little of your history,

00:03:00.914 --> 00:03:02.148
which is pretty amazing,

00:03:02.148 --> 00:03:03.082
and you've done
some great stuff,

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.817
let's talk about Maxine Waters,

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:07.187
because in the ad you
talk about the fact

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:10.490
that she lives in a
$6 million mansion

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:13.026
that is not in that district.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:15.161
If I'm not mistaken,
she's in Hancock Park,

00:03:15.161 --> 00:03:18.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is a pretty swanky,
swanky area of LA.

00:03:18.231 --> 00:03:19.165
(Joe laughs)

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.167
Obviously not South Central.

00:03:21.167 --> 00:03:23.236
But that she's also
been in business,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:26.573
and by business, I mean
government, for 44 years.

00:03:26.573 --> 00:03:30.043
How did she get a
$6 million mansion?

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:32.879 align:start size:97% position:3%
Which I don't begrudge someone
earning money honestly,

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:34.547 align:start size:81% position:19%
but in 44 years
of public service,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:35.548
you usually don't
think of someone

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.016
getting a $6 million mansion.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:39.619
- Yeah, you know, she
has a ton of mansions.

00:03:39.619 --> 00:03:41.688
And from doing research,

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.157
I've seen a lot of backhanded
things that she's been doing,

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.759
you know, pocket padding and
all that other type of stuff.

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:50.096 align:start size:97% position:3%
And we have to say, you know,
it has to be corruption.

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:52.832
She's been labeled the most
corrupt politician five times

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:55.101
by the Citizens for
Ethics Committee.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:59.372
She has her own page
in the Judicial Watch

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:01.541 line:0%
called career corruption.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:03.509 line:0%
And it features Maxine Waters

00:04:03.509 --> 00:04:04.744 line:0%
and everything she's been doing.

00:04:04.744 --> 00:04:07.080 line:0%
She's gotten a lot
of backhanded deals.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:10.416 align:start position:0%
She's even ripped off
politicians here in California.

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.987
They pay her $45,000
for an endorsement

00:04:13.987 --> 00:04:15.989 align:start size:84% position:16%
and another, you
know, 10, 15, $20,000

00:04:15.989 --> 00:04:18.791
to get on her slate mailer
scheme that she has going.

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:20.193
So, I mean,

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.228 align:start size:97% position:3%
when it comes to the
corruption of Maxine Waters,

00:04:22.228 --> 00:04:23.596
it knows no limit.

00:04:23.596 --> 00:04:24.864
- Yeah, so, all right.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.466
I don't want to get
too lost on Maxine.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:97% position:3%
'Cause I think your feelings
about her are clear.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.104
And I have a feeling
most of my audience

00:04:31.104 --> 00:04:32.038 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably agrees with you.
(Joe laughs)

00:04:32.038 --> 00:04:33.273
But let's talk about you.

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:35.908
Because I don't think
most people think that,

00:04:35.908 --> 00:04:38.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wait, a Black Republican
from South Central?

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:40.913
Could that possibly exist?"

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.382
Now we know a lot of stereotypes

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.916
are being broken these days,

00:04:43.916 --> 00:04:46.953 align:start size:97% position:3%
but can you tell me a little
bit about your history?

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
- So yeah, I'm from South
Central Los Angeles.

00:04:48.755 --> 00:04:50.923
I was born and raised there

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.692 align:start size:84% position:16%
and we ended up having
to move to Texas

00:04:52.692 --> 00:04:54.827 align:start size:84% position:16%
after my house was
shot up in a drive-by.

00:04:54.827 --> 00:04:56.129
So I was already in high school.

00:04:56.129 --> 00:04:57.697
So I ended up finishing
high school in Texas.

00:04:57.697 --> 00:05:00.667 align:start size:88% position:13%
I graduated in 2003,
joined the Navy in 2004.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:02.402 align:start size:84% position:16%
That's where I
became a Republican.

00:05:02.402 --> 00:05:03.836
And the reason why is because

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.539
in the history of Black people,

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:09.642 align:start position:0%
we see that the first Black
men to get involved in politics

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:11.044
were Republicans.

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:13.146 align:start size:97% position:3%
And that's what the
Republican party stood for,

00:05:13.146 --> 00:05:16.482
freedom, antislavery,
fight for your rights,

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:81% position:19%
and that's what
resonated with me.

00:05:19.719 --> 00:05:23.656
- So what possessed you to
possibly go into politics?

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.792
You come back after the Navy

00:05:25.792 --> 00:05:27.360
and what possessed you to say,

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
"All right, I'm gonna
throw my hat in the ring."

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.564
- I actually got
out the military

00:05:31.564 --> 00:05:32.732
to get involved in politics.

00:05:32.732 --> 00:05:35.234 align:start size:88% position:13%
I got an administrative
separation general

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.469
under honorable conditions

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.004
so I can pursue a
career in politics.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:41.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it was because,
through the 2016 election,

00:05:41.808 --> 00:05:43.810 align:start size:97% position:3%
the voice of the younger
people were not being heard.

00:05:43.810 --> 00:05:45.545
And everybody called
us lazy millennials.

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.413
They called us lazy, they
said we were worthless,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:48.948
we couldn't do anything.

00:05:48.948 --> 00:05:52.385
And mind you, in the Navy and
the entire military in itself,

00:05:52.385 --> 00:05:54.153
it's about 4 million millennials

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.289 align:start size:97% position:3%
that wake up every day at
four o'clock in the morning.

00:05:56.289 --> 00:05:57.590 align:start size:84% position:16%
We do more in between
four and eight

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.892
than most people do all day.

00:05:59.892 --> 00:06:02.895 align:start size:97% position:3%
And so whenever we would
bring our issues to the table,

00:06:02.895 --> 00:06:04.764
they would say, "Wait," or
"It's not your turn yet,"

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:05.865
or "We're gonna take
care of it for you,"

00:06:05.865 --> 00:06:07.100
but our voice was never heard.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:08.968
And so I wanted our
voice to be heard.

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I got out the military,
hopped into politics.

00:06:11.304 --> 00:06:13.873
I actually started off as
a presidential candidate.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:16.642 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, you know, after
I learned a lot,

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.177
because, you know,

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.445
you can't get involved in
politics in the military.

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:20.980
So I learned a lot as a
presidential candidate.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:23.349
Then I started the race
to run for Congress.

00:06:23.349 --> 00:06:25.418
And part of that reason was
because of Maxine Waters,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:28.020
trying to get help
with my VA benefits.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.622 align:start size:84% position:16%
I was sleeping
outside the lighthouse

00:06:29.622 --> 00:06:30.923
at Ranchos Palos Verdes.

00:06:30.923 --> 00:06:32.592
And I was going to her
office every other day,

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.960
trying to get help.

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:35.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
I filled out job
applications, internships,

00:06:35.495 --> 00:06:36.529
I even brought her flowers.

00:06:36.529 --> 00:06:38.398
And I was met with silence.

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:40.133
And that really made me upset

00:06:40.133 --> 00:06:42.301 align:start size:97% position:3%
because the majority of the
people who live on the streets

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.605
are homeless veterans and
60% of them are Black.

00:06:45.605 --> 00:06:47.039 align:start size:84% position:16%
And so you have
this lady who says,

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:48.875
"Well, I'm pro Black
this, pro Black that,

00:06:48.875 --> 00:06:49.709
I fight for Black people,"

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:50.643
all of this stuff.

00:06:50.643 --> 00:06:52.011
And here I am, a young Black man

00:06:52.011 --> 00:06:53.246
and you're not fighting for me.

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:56.182
We have 44,000 homeless
people on the street.

00:06:56.182 --> 00:06:58.217
60% of them are Black veterans.

00:06:58.217 --> 00:06:59.719
You're not fighting
for those people.

00:06:59.719 --> 00:07:02.255
So which Black people are
you fighting for, you know?

00:07:02.255 --> 00:07:04.624
And so she has to, she gotta go.

00:07:04.624 --> 00:07:05.792
- Yeah.

00:07:05.792 --> 00:07:08.060 align:start size:88% position:13%
So why is it, you know,
I'm in LA as well.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:10.563
And why is it, do you think,

00:07:10.563 --> 00:07:13.099 align:start size:97% position:3%
that people in LA, and
really California as a whole,

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.368
but I think LA and San
Francisco specifically,

00:07:15.368 --> 00:07:17.904
seem unable to connect the dots

00:07:17.904 --> 00:07:21.240 align:start size:84% position:16%
between always
voting in Democrats

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.909
and things always getting worse.

00:07:22.909 --> 00:07:24.744
They seem to not
be able to realize,

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.113 align:start size:81% position:19%
"Oh, we keep doing
the same thing

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.815
and things keep going
the wrong direction.

00:07:28.815 --> 00:07:30.416 align:start size:84% position:16%
Maybe we gotta vote
in some other people."

00:07:30.416 --> 00:07:32.652
Have you figured
out why that is?

00:07:32.652 --> 00:07:35.021
- I think it's because,

00:07:35.021 --> 00:07:36.255
when it comes to politics

00:07:36.255 --> 00:07:38.324
and this is something
that I've noticed,

00:07:38.324 --> 00:07:40.626 align:start size:97% position:3%
you know, a lot of
candidates don't run to win.

00:07:40.626 --> 00:07:41.861
They want to be famous,

00:07:41.861 --> 00:07:43.329
they wanna be social
media influencers.

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:45.331 align:start size:97% position:3%
So they don't put in the
necessary work that it takes

00:07:45.331 --> 00:07:49.435 align:start position:0%
to win a campaign, to raise
money to get their messages out.

00:07:49.435 --> 00:07:52.138
And so that's what we've been
seeing for a very long time.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.372
People want change,

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:54.841
but if they don't
know you exist,

00:07:54.841 --> 00:07:56.309
they can't vote for you.

00:07:56.309 --> 00:07:57.543
- Yeah.

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.412
So what are the things
that you want to do?

00:07:59.412 --> 00:08:02.181
I mean, we all know the
homeless situation in LA

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:05.384 align:start size:97% position:3%
is just, it almost seems like
every week it gets worse.

00:08:05.384 --> 00:08:07.053
What are some of like the hard,

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:10.156
give me like three, four
of just the linchpin things

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:11.157
that you want to accomplish

00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:12.859
and how you're gonna do it.

00:08:12.859 --> 00:08:15.127
- Okay, well, I have
my five point plan

00:08:15.127 --> 00:08:16.529
and the reason why I came up--

00:08:16.529 --> 00:08:19.232 align:start size:88% position:13%
- I'll go with all
five, let's do all five.

00:08:19.232 --> 00:08:20.466
- (laughs) All right.

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:21.868
So I want to rebuild
the infrastructure

00:08:21.868 --> 00:08:24.837 align:start size:88% position:13%
to support the expansion
of small businesses,

00:08:24.837 --> 00:08:26.305
as well as housing.

00:08:26.305 --> 00:08:28.174
I want to overhaul the education

00:08:28.174 --> 00:08:30.743
and start rebuilding our high
schools in the 43rd district.

00:08:30.743 --> 00:08:32.879 align:start size:81% position:19%
I want to bring
quality jobs back.

00:08:32.879 --> 00:08:34.847
Improve the relationship
between the law enforcement

00:08:34.847 --> 00:08:36.115
and the community.

00:08:36.115 --> 00:08:38.084 line:0%
And I also want to bring
financial literacy back.

00:08:38.084 --> 00:08:39.385 line:0%
And these are just basics,

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:40.720 line:0%
basic things that you need

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:43.623 align:start size:97% position:3% line:0%
in order to have a
productive, positive society.

00:08:43.623 --> 00:08:45.491
So we have to get
back to the basics.

00:08:45.491 --> 00:08:47.960 align:start size:84% position:16%
And, you know, you
asked, how I'ma do it?

00:08:47.960 --> 00:08:49.228
It's easy.

00:08:49.228 --> 00:08:50.863
You just go to work
and you do your job.

00:08:50.863 --> 00:08:52.565
And I know that on
a private capacity,

00:08:52.565 --> 00:08:55.001
what we've been able to
do with the campaign,

00:08:55.001 --> 00:08:57.103
what I've been able to
do in the community,

00:08:57.103 --> 00:08:59.438
as far as bringing jobs and
taking care of our community

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:01.574
through COVID-19 is
absolutely possible.

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:03.776
And it's easy, you just
have to want to do it.

00:09:03.776 --> 00:09:05.044
- Yeah.

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:06.546
Let's talk about the
policing situation,

00:09:06.546 --> 00:09:08.381 align:start size:97% position:3%
because obviously everyone's
talking about that

00:09:08.381 --> 00:09:09.582
all the time.

00:09:09.582 --> 00:09:11.751
What do you make
about the relations

00:09:11.751 --> 00:09:13.419
between the police and,

00:09:13.419 --> 00:09:15.421
I hate phrases like
the Black community,

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:17.256
but, you know, with at least

00:09:17.256 --> 00:09:19.458 align:start size:88% position:13%
the constituents in
your district right now.

00:09:20.326 --> 00:09:21.394
- You know, it's kind of tough

00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:24.230
because everybody overemphasizes

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.466 align:start size:94% position:6%
the issues of police
brutality in inner cities,

00:09:27.466 --> 00:09:29.602
and they ignore everything else

00:09:29.602 --> 00:09:31.470
that we have going on
in our communities.

00:09:31.470 --> 00:09:34.607
And a lot of times, you
know, when you hear,

00:09:34.607 --> 00:09:37.743
"Oh, a Black person was shot
by a cop, it has to be racism."

00:09:37.743 --> 00:09:39.111
Even though the cop
was either Black

00:09:39.111 --> 00:09:42.448 align:start size:84% position:16%
or the cop was Latino
who shot the guy,

00:09:42.448 --> 00:09:44.317 align:start size:84% position:16%
it has to be racist
for some point.

00:09:44.317 --> 00:09:45.818
And then they always point out,

00:09:45.818 --> 00:09:47.920
"Well, cops did this, and
cops do that all the time."

00:09:47.920 --> 00:09:49.488
And having someone
like Maxine Waters

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.624 align:start size:88% position:13%
come in to the community
doesn't make it easy.

00:09:51.624 --> 00:09:53.459
Having organizations
like Black Lives Matter

00:09:53.459 --> 00:09:55.161
coming into the community
doesn't make it any easy

00:09:55.161 --> 00:09:58.664
because, you know, if we have
such an issue with police,

00:09:58.664 --> 00:10:00.733 align:start size:97% position:3%
then what we need to be
working on is police reform.

00:10:00.733 --> 00:10:01.867
We need to get social training

00:10:01.867 --> 00:10:03.903
within our police departments.

00:10:03.903 --> 00:10:05.538
We need to get better
oversight committees

00:10:05.538 --> 00:10:06.606
within our police department.

00:10:06.606 --> 00:10:08.074
We need to increase the budget

00:10:08.074 --> 00:10:10.276 align:start size:97% position:3%
so we can have better training
for our police department.

00:10:10.276 --> 00:10:11.444
And these aren't things

00:10:11.444 --> 00:10:12.445 align:start size:84% position:16%
that people are
bringing to the table,

00:10:12.445 --> 00:10:13.679
but these are things

00:10:13.679 --> 00:10:15.815
that I've been able to
work with the mayor on.

00:10:15.815 --> 00:10:17.717
And we were doing
a really good job.

00:10:17.717 --> 00:10:19.051 align:start size:84% position:16%
So we've been
standing in the gap

00:10:19.051 --> 00:10:21.020 align:start size:97% position:3%
between the police
department and the community,

00:10:21.020 --> 00:10:22.455
making sure things stay calm.

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:24.090
And a lot of people
from the, you know,

00:10:24.090 --> 00:10:26.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
Black Lives Matter
organization don't like it

00:10:26.025 --> 00:10:29.161 align:start size:88% position:13%
because they raise money
off hatred and fear.

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:30.730
But at the end of the day,

00:10:30.730 --> 00:10:32.865 align:start size:84% position:16%
when it comes to
taking responsibility
for the community,

00:10:32.865 --> 00:10:34.033
this is something
that, you know,

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:36.369
me and my team has been doing.

00:10:36.369 --> 00:10:37.603
- Yeah.

00:10:37.603 --> 00:10:40.139 align:start size:84% position:16%
So I'm not a huge
fan of Eric Garcetti,

00:10:40.139 --> 00:10:42.241 align:start size:84% position:16%
our mayor here in LA.
(Joe laughs)

00:10:42.241 --> 00:10:44.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do you want to try to sell
me on him a little bit?

00:10:44.176 --> 00:10:45.444
Or is this just one thing

00:10:45.444 --> 00:10:47.713
you've been able to
work with him on?

00:10:47.713 --> 00:10:50.650
- No, I'm not gonna sell
anybody on Mayor Garcetti,

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:52.918
'cause he's never
sold anybody on me.

00:10:52.918 --> 00:10:54.820
But I think, when you're
in a leadership position,

00:10:54.820 --> 00:10:56.022
it is your obligation

00:10:56.022 --> 00:10:57.657 align:start size:84% position:16%
to work with the
people who are leaders

00:10:57.657 --> 00:10:59.225 align:start size:81% position:19%
in order to affect
better change.

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:01.293
And I don't have a problem
with working with anybody

00:11:01.293 --> 00:11:03.796
if it's gonna create some
type of positive change.

00:11:03.796 --> 00:11:05.031
Do I like him personally?

00:11:05.031 --> 00:11:05.865
Maybe.

00:11:05.865 --> 00:11:07.333
He's a U.S. Navy sailor.

00:11:07.333 --> 00:11:08.601
Do I like his policies?

00:11:08.601 --> 00:11:10.169
You know, sometimes I
do, sometimes I don't,

00:11:10.169 --> 00:11:11.437
but at the end of the day,

00:11:11.437 --> 00:11:15.341
if we could take some
type of medium ground

00:11:15.341 --> 00:11:16.742
to build some type
of relationships

00:11:16.742 --> 00:11:18.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
to improve our
communities, I'm with it.

00:11:18.711 --> 00:11:19.645
- Yeah.

00:11:19.645 --> 00:11:21.180
So backing up for just a sec,

00:11:21.180 --> 00:11:24.650
when you hear people talk
about defunding the police

00:11:24.650 --> 00:11:25.918
and everything else,

00:11:25.918 --> 00:11:27.186
I've heard, a lot of
people basically say

00:11:27.186 --> 00:11:29.221
this is just like
a media construct.

00:11:29.221 --> 00:11:31.223 align:start size:81% position:19%
Like nobody really
wants it done.

00:11:31.223 --> 00:11:33.225 align:start size:88% position:13%
Is that what you're
hearing from your folks?

00:11:33.225 --> 00:11:34.694
(Joe laughs)

00:11:34.694 --> 00:11:36.729 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Nobody's going to defund
the police department.

00:11:36.729 --> 00:11:38.631
I mean, when you look at
the amount of gang violence

00:11:38.631 --> 00:11:40.266
and gun violence,
domestic violence,

00:11:40.266 --> 00:11:42.068
and drugs and alcohol
related incidents,

00:11:42.068 --> 00:11:45.938
and, you know, all these
cases in our communities,

00:11:45.938 --> 00:11:47.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
you absolutely don't want
to defund the police.

00:11:47.907 --> 00:11:49.175
The crazy part about it is

00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:51.544
the same people who talk
about defunding police

00:11:51.544 --> 00:11:53.112
are the same people
who call the police

00:11:53.112 --> 00:11:54.480 align:start size:84% position:16%
when something happens
to 'em, you know?

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:55.981
So it's never gonna happen.

00:11:55.981 --> 00:11:57.516
It's like a red herring.

00:11:57.516 --> 00:11:59.218
It's the dumbest thing I've
ever heard in my entire life.

00:11:59.218 --> 00:12:00.052
- Yeah.

00:12:00.052 --> 00:12:01.320
What do you make about

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.055
just the general state
of politics right now?

00:12:03.055 --> 00:12:05.658
Not just your district,
not just Maxine Waters,

00:12:05.658 --> 00:12:08.527
but like what's happening
nationally, Trump, Biden,

00:12:08.527 --> 00:12:13.499
the over and intense focus
on politics all day long.

00:12:13.499 --> 00:12:15.367 align:start size:84% position:16%
What do you think?
- I think it's a mess.

00:12:15.367 --> 00:12:18.337
I think this is the complete
reason why we need term limits.

00:12:18.337 --> 00:12:21.207
We have politicians who
refuse to work together.

00:12:21.207 --> 00:12:22.675
Everybody want to be right,

00:12:22.675 --> 00:12:24.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they're trying to
implement the same things

00:12:24.376 --> 00:12:26.078
that they had in
the '70s and '80s.

00:12:26.078 --> 00:12:28.214 align:start size:88% position:13%
It didn't work then,
it's not gonna work now.

00:12:28.214 --> 00:12:29.648 align:start size:88% position:13%
And we have a president
who's struggling

00:12:29.648 --> 00:12:31.951
trying to get things
done for our country.

00:12:31.951 --> 00:12:33.719 line:0%
And, you know, people just
don't want to work together.

00:12:33.719 --> 00:12:36.622 line:0%
So we got to get these
people out of office

00:12:36.622 --> 00:12:38.057 line:0%
on every single level.

00:12:38.057 --> 00:12:40.826 align:start position:0% line:0%
At some point, these politicians
should have been aged out

00:12:40.826 --> 00:12:42.194 line:0%
and created an avenue

00:12:42.194 --> 00:12:45.531 align:start size:97% position:3%
for new, younger politicians
with fresh ideas.

00:12:45.531 --> 00:12:46.766
- Yeah, all right.

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:48.300 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, listen, I wish
we had more time,

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:50.970
but we did this one on the
fly, just cause I saw the ad

00:12:50.970 --> 00:12:52.371 align:start size:84% position:16%
and I wanted to help
get the word out.

00:12:52.371 --> 00:12:55.274
I hope to see you
in real life in LA.

00:12:55.274 --> 00:12:57.510
Your neighborhood or
mine is fine with me.

00:12:57.510 --> 00:12:59.011 align:start size:81% position:19%
For people that
want to follow you

00:12:59.011 --> 00:13:02.181 align:start size:97% position:3%
and help you before election
time, where can they go?

00:13:02.181 --> 00:13:04.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
- My website is
joecollinsforcongress.com.

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:06.218 align:start size:84% position:16%
You can find me on
Facebook and Instagram

00:13:06.218 --> 00:13:08.154
at @collinsforcongress43.

00:13:08.154 --> 00:13:10.990
And you can find me at
Twitter @joecollins43rd.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.024
- And Joe, you got to hook me up

00:13:12.024 --> 00:13:13.292
with the guy who did that video,

00:13:13.292 --> 00:13:15.861
'cause I need some slick
branding like that, man.

00:13:17.029 --> 00:13:18.731 align:start size:81% position:19%
- All right, I got
you, I got you.

00:13:18.731 --> 00:13:20.399
- All right, thanks a lot, Joe.

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:21.867
- All right, talk to you later.

